1 TITL Captain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lars Amundsen was born in Fredrikshald on December 30, 1784, and had his schooling in the birthplace. Immediately after the confirmation he went to sea and spent time on the brigade 'Amitie' of Fredrikshald. This w
2 CONC as at 40 "kommerselester" (a measurement of a ships capacity) and belonged to Wholesaler Truls Wiel. Skipper was Johannes Olsen, Barm, Vesterøy. He was Lars Amundsen's uncle. The crew was 6 people. Lars Amundsen took a mate's exam
2 CONC  in Christiania on February 27, 1807, and a ship's certificate on 5 February 1811. He received a "skipperborgerskap" in Fredrikshald fourteen days later, and on March 18, he became the leader of the ship "Cornelius & Jan" at 114 "
2 CONC kommerselester". His first trip as a skipper went to Bordeaux, France. Wholesalers Carsten Tank and Rasmus Leganger owned the ship, which Lars Amundsen was on board for well 3 years.
2 CONT
