1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Clara Matilda Amundsen was born in North Dakota, the oldest of many children. With parents and relatives struggling to re-establish themselves after leaving Norway, Clara would have first learned Norweigian and abo
2 CONC ut the Luthern ways. Helping the the younger children and chores, would have been a priority, especially when they followed their adventurous father into Southern Alberta. Clara  and JT North, who went into partnership for awhile 
2 CONC with Clara's father, Ole, were married in Sept of 1907. Clara was 25 years old and JT was 30. Clara was 5 foot 2 inches, light blue eyes and brown hair and J.T. was 5 feet 11 inches tall, with grey brown eyes and dark hair (accord
2 CONC ing to a joint passport issued in 1941 so they could visit the States). They moved to Parkland in 1909 where he farmed and operated Amundsen and North Realty. So after the birth of their third child, they moved to Calgary, where h
2 CONC er husband taught school, preached, sold insurance, was often quoted in the newspaper, and organized social and political events. They were both committed to Wesley United (formerly a Methodist) church. In addition to raising her 
2 CONC six children, Clara took in boarders, and accounted for every penny she spent.  Clara's diabetes went undiscovered for too many years and caused her grief, but she still had a soft word for all. 
