1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lena was travelling home to Claresholm with her parents Ole & Mary. The family was the first to own an automobile in Claresholm. Their car was in an accident on a bridge, Lena ran to the nearest farm for help. The 
2 CONC closest telephone was 3 miles away so the farmers daughter rode a horse to telephone for an ambulance. But Ole & Mary had died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sunday, Dec. 29, 1918 - Midnapore, Alberta
2 CONT
2 CONT Lena was travelling home to Claresholm with her parents Ole & Mary. The family was the first to own an automobile in Claresholm. Their car was in an accident on a bridge, Lena ran to the nearest farm for help. The closest telephon
2 CONC e was 3 miles away so the farmers daughter rode a horse to telephone for an ambulance. Ole died at the scene & Mary died later in the hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT
