1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Martin and Randina Thompson and the family emigrated from Veldre, Norway May 5, 1901. The family first arrived in Devil's lake North Dakota to join relatives who had come out several years earlier.
2 CONT
2 CONT After spending a year in Devil's Lake, in the fall of 1902 they left North Dakota and arrived by train in Claresholm on November 18, 1902. They had travelled to Claresholm with several families, including Martin's parents (Nels Th
2 CONC ompson), Mr. & Mrs August Foss and family, Mr & Mrs Ole Amundsen and family, and Mr & Mrs Tom Benson and family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin and Randina had five surviving children; Ole, Karen, Nettie, Nels and Martha. Two infant sons passed away in Norway prior to the family's immigration to the US.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first few months in Claresholm were spent in town. They homesteaded the NW 1/4 section 34-12-27, a mile northwest of the town. They moved onto the homestead in January of 1903, even though the house was not completed until som
2 CONC etime later. At a later date, Martin and Ole Bilben bought southwest quater of the same section, with Martin buying out Ole's share after a time to become the sole owner.
2 CONT
2 CONT In May 1903, Randina passed away and the oldest daughter, Karen at age 13, was left to take care of her brothers and sisters. Martin worked for the CPR as well as farming his land.
2 CONT
2 CONT As water was unavailable on the farm, the children hauled water by the barrel with a horse and stone boat from a slough. Lack of good water was always a problem on the farm and many wells were dug - most of them unsuccessful. Kare
2 CONC n tells of an episode which occurred when she was helping her father dig one of the wells. Martin had gone down the well to light a stick of dynamite, as he started up the ladder, the ladder broke. He barely made it over the top w
2 CONC hen the dynamite blew. Fortunately neither Karen or Martin were injured.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin remained on his farm until his passing in 1943 at the age of 79.
2 CONT
2 CONT
