1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Teasdale North was known as Jack and as JT. He attended teacher's college in Truro, NS and taught in several locations before moving West. He was a student minister for a time in Southern Alberta, then took up
2 CONC  teaching again. He was a poet, an orator, a lay minister, an advocate for many causes, including amateur hockey, and was founder of the parent-teacher association in Calgary. 
