1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bev played hockey in 1938 for Olds Elks of the Alberta Senior Hockey League and left after that season, at age 22. Bev had been recruited by Arnold Eddy, Trojans ice hockey coach, and given an athletic scholarship 
2 CONC at the University of Southern California, graduating in 1941 with a bachelor of science in accounting and his letter in hockey for 1939-40-41. He also took on small movie parts including skating numbers. His most notable performan
2 CONC ce was in the picture The Duke of West Point in which he had a speaking part.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://sportsillustrated.cnn.com/vault/article/magazine/MAG1066674/1/index.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Second Lieut. North joined the United States air force and was assigned to the USAAF Central Flying Training Command as an auditor.   Bev married Marilee, whose father, Bruce Macy, was business manager of the Camarillio State Ment
2 CONC al Hospital. Bev, 32, had a brain haemorrhage at 1000 sitting at his desk at California Signal Oil in Alhambra.
