1 NOTE {geni:about_me} “Kathie”, or “Kaye” went to business college and worked for Burns and for GSL. She made dozens of friends and was always determined to make a good time. She married LAC John Ogilvie Brown on April 19, 1943.  Aunt E
2 CONC thel played the organ at the ceremony at Wesley United, Louise Gidman was a flower girl, and the reception was back at 812 14 Ave SW.  Kath and her husband were stationed to Montreal, where his mother still lived. They travelled a
2 CONC fter the war, had lots of dinner parties and then divorced, with Brownie going to New Zealand. Kath moved back to the little house at 1509 14 Av SW with her German Shepard to look after Clara. Kay was the one who went off to Norwa
2 CONC y on a search for Clara’s relatives and visited often with cousins. Kathie then moved to Bow View Manor, was on oxygen, built wonderful clay nativity scenes, continued smoking, and died of emphysema.  Kathie did have many old pict
2 CONC ures which she entrusted to John and Linda. 
